          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Equivariant complex oriented cohomology theory
            is the generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
          %p
            In generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            as the prototypical example of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            is equivariantly complex oriented.
