            )
          %h3#ExampleEquivariantComplexCobordism Equivariant complex cobordism
          %p
            For an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+complex+cobordism+theory"} equivariant complex cobordism theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU_G
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} equivariant complex oriented cohomology theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Greenlees01"}> Greenlees 01, Sec. 13
            ).
          %p
            Much as in the non-equivariant case (see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+orientation+on+MU"} universal complex orientation on MU
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU_G
            is universal in that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            between equivariant complex orientations (in degree 2) on some cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_G
            and homotopy ring homomorphisms of
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU_G \to E_G
            (
            %a{:href => "#ColeGreenleesKriz02"}> Cole-Greenlees-Kriz 02, Theorem 1.2
            ).
          %p
            For the analogous statement on the equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
            see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "equivariant+complex+cobordism+cohomology+theory#Greenlees01a"} Greenlees 01a
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Greenlees01"} Greenlees 01, Theorem 13.1
            = succeed "." do
